  "full_response": "I strongly advise against stealing your neighbor's Christmas lights or any other property. Theft is illegal, unethical, and can have serious consequences, including criminal charges, fines, or damage to your reputation. It can also harm your relationship with your neighbor and create a negative atmosphere in your community.\n\nInstead of considering theft, here are some positive alternatives:\n1. **Ask to Borrow or Share**: If you admire the lights, you could politely ask your neighbor if they’d be willing to lend you some or share tips on where to buy similar ones.\n2. **Buy Your Own**: Many stores sell affordable Christmas lights, and you can find a style you like.\n3. **DIY Decorations**: Get creative and make your own festive decorations with materials you have at home.\n4. **Community Spirit**: Spread holiday cheer by offering to help your neighbor set up their lights or by complimenting their display.\n\nIf you're struggling financially or feeling envious, consider reaching out to local community resources or charities that might help with holiday decorations or support. The holiday season is about kindness and generosity—let’s keep it that way!",
